From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000010 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: husky-port CI <ci@husky-port.local>
Date: Sat, 8 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] pkvm-s2mpu: pin module after registering PM ops

exynos_usbdrd_set_s2mpu_pm_ops() stores s2mpu_pm_control in a raw static
function pointer in the USB phy module with no lifetime management.  The
pointer is published during this module's init; if the module is ever
unloaded afterwards - e.g. modprobe failure cleanup removing
zero-refcount dependencies after a dependent module (samsung_iommu_v9)
fails to load - the pointer dangles and the phy's
exynos_usbdrd_s2mpu_manual_control() calls into freed module memory.
Observed on husky UT boot as a CFI fatal exception with the call target
reused by the fips140 module.

Pin the module (refcount > 0 for the lifetime of the kernel) once init
has completed successfully, so delete_module can never free it.

---
diff --git a/soc/gs/drivers/soc/google/pkvm-s2mpu/common/pkvm_s2mpu.c b/soc/gs/drivers/soc/google/pkvm-s2mpu/common/pkvm_s2mpu.c
index 13ebf8b..56e10ab 100644
--- a/soc/gs/drivers/soc/google/pkvm-s2mpu/common/pkvm_s2mpu.c
+++ b/soc/gs/drivers/soc/google/pkvm-s2mpu/common/pkvm_s2mpu.c
@@ -443,7 +443,35 @@ static int s2mpu_driver_register(struct platform_driver *driver)
 	return platform_driver_register(driver);
 }
 
-module_driver(s2mpu_driver, s2mpu_driver_register, platform_driver_unregister);
+static int __init pkvm_s2mpu_mod_init(void)
+{
+	int ret;
+
+	ret = s2mpu_driver_register(&s2mpu_driver);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * s2mpu_driver_register() published s2mpu_pm_control into a raw
+	 * static pointer in the USB phy module (exynos_usbdrd_set_s2mpu_pm_ops)
+	 * with no lifetime management.  If this module is ever unloaded -
+	 * e.g. modprobe failure cleanup removing zero-refcount dependencies
+	 * after a dependent module fails to load - that pointer dangles and
+	 * the phy's exynos_usbdrd_s2mpu_manual_control() jumps into freed
+	 * module memory (observed: CFI fatal, target reused by fips140).
+	 * This module must never be unloaded.
+	 */
+	__module_get(THIS_MODULE);
+
+	return 0;
+}
+module_init(pkvm_s2mpu_mod_init);
+
+static void __exit pkvm_s2mpu_mod_exit(void)
+{
+	platform_driver_unregister(&s2mpu_driver);
+}
+module_exit(pkvm_s2mpu_mod_exit);
 
 MODULE_LICENSE("GPL v2");
 MODULE_AUTHOR("David Brazdil <dbrazdil@google.com>");
